he normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, the Section 4 wrapper rule and Section 7.5 LeaseToken).\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Spec fidelity — quote the pinned clauses for each gate (activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, restore, terminate-stale) and the park vocabulary (session.parked reasons remote_owner|stale_owner|restore_policy|failed_handoff; stale_fenced) and diff them against gate.go/terminate.go; confirm every refusal uses a registered Section 15 class with its exact exit through internal/axerror (the producer claims 10/10/10/2/3 — enumerate which sentinel maps to which class and check none is newly minted); confirm terminate-stale is admitted only under explicit force recovery and refused otherwise. (2) Refusal census — enumerate every refusal/park arm of Authorize* and Bind; each needs a named test reaching it through the production entry; attack the taxonomy: swap two adjacent arms sharing a class, swallow one arm into its sibling with a one-token edit, delete a park branch so the gate refuses instead of parks — the suite must go RED for each; report n-of-m with call sites. (3) Own plants through the production entries — lower epoch by one and by many, same-epoch loser with a lease_id that sorts before and after the winner, foreign session with the winner's epoch, expired grant at the boundary second (CheckFencingExpiry off-by-one), absent lease with a stale checkpoint present, ambiguous ownership (two same-epoch candidates), remote owner with a locally cached older lease, unverified sync state, old-owner reconnect after force takeover (losing token rejected, divergent history preserved through the sessstate union), two concurrent force takeovers (deterministic winner, loser history retained), a minted LeaseToken replayed for a different operation, a token bound for epoch N presented after a CAS to N+1; record admitted/refused/parked with the exact class and reason for each. (4) Forgery bound — the LeaseToken must be unforgeable outside the package: attempt construction from another package (unexported fields, no exported constructor, method value/reflection excluded by convention — say what the census covers), rerun TestLeaseTokenCensusPlants with your own plant shapes (an alias type, a composite literal through an unexported-field embedding, a var binding, a build-tagged file, a generic wrapper) and confirm the census refuses each; confirm the testdata/forge and testdata/use controls do what they claim. (5) Mutation — rerun testdata/mutate.py in an isolated copy, rerun each of the 31 KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) Agreement — the exhaustive 144-pair enumeration must cover the full small alphabet (epochs {1,2,3} × lease IDs {x,y} × holders {a,b} per side); plant a tie-break divergence on each side and confirm it goes RED; confirm created_at is diagnostic-only per the pinned text. (7) Traceability and docs — the ownership registry changes (section:5.3 to CompareAndSwapLease 7/8 partial with clause 5.3#5 open, section:2.2 sliver 4/22 to Authorize, 9 acceptance cases, digest re-pin): recompute the projection digest independently, confirm every claimed clause line exists in the pinned document, confirm no self-minted claim (each binding names an existing production declaration with an acceptance case that drives it), tracecheck 28/485 reproduced; README figures/prose and LOGBOOK truthful, no CLI/capability claim; the residual section:17.2 nit correctly out of scope. (8) Hygiene — changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; go vet, gofmt clean; go test ./internal/fencing ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessstate ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and catalog