n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Spec fidelity — quote the pinned clauses for each gate (activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, restore, terminate-stale) and the park vocabulary (session.parked reasons remote_owner|stale_owner|restore_policy|failed_handoff; stale_fenced) and diff them against gate.go/terminate.go; confirm every refusal uses a registered Section 15 class with its exact exit through internal/axerror (the producer claims 10/10/10/2/3 — enumerate which sentinel maps to which class and check none is newly minted); confirm terminate-stale is admitted only under explicit force recovery and refused otherwise. (2) Refusal census — enumerate every refusal/park arm of Authorize* and Bind; each needs a named test reaching it through the production entry; attack the taxonomy: swap two adjacent arms sharing a class, swallow one arm into its sibling with a one-token edit, delete a park branch so the gate refuses instead of parks — the suite must go RED for each; report n-of-m with call sites. (3) Own plants through the production entries — lower epoch by one and by many, same-epoch loser with a lease_id that sorts before and after the winner, foreign session with the winner's epoch, expired grant at the boundary second (CheckFencingExpiry off-by-one), absent lease with a stale checkpoint present, ambiguous ownership (two same-epoch candidates), remote owner with a locally cached older lease, unverified sync state, old-owner reconnect after force takeover (losing token rejected, divergent history preserved through the sessstate union), two concurrent force takeovers (deterministic winner, loser history retained), a minted LeaseToken replayed for a different operation, a token bound for epoch N presented after a CAS to N+1; record admitted/refused/parked with the exact class and reason for each. (4) Forgery bound — the LeaseToken must be unforgeable outside the package: attempt construction from another package (unexported fields, no exported constructor, 