{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":544,"recorded_at":1780531400001083,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae3b-e664-7a03-b8a7-130cfc4d923d"},"task_id":"01a0ae3b-e664-7a03-b8a7-130cfc4d923d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae3b-e664-7a03-b8a7-130cfc4d923d","chunk":"Read text file `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n1|name: CI\n2|\n3|on:\n4|  pull_request:\n5|  push:\n6|    branches:\n7|      - main\n8|\n9|permissions:\n10|  contents: read\n11|\n12|# What green means. Every job below proves its selection matched something:\n13|# a grep, glob, file scan, matrix expansion, or test selector that finds\n14|# nothing fails closed instead of passing on an empty result set. No job\n15|# declares an `if:` condition, so no job can skip quietly; gates-verdict\n16|# additionally refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\n17|#\n18|# GOOS=windows work is compile-and-vet only. A green windows-compile-only job\n19|# proves the tree type-checks for Windows; it never implies executed\n20|# behaviour. Coverage is reported as numbers, not enforced as a floor.\n21|jobs:\n22|  contract-preservation:\n23|    name: Contract preservation (v0.5.0 current, v0.4.3 historical)\n24|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n25|    timeout-minutes: 10\n26|    steps:\n27|      - name: Check out repository\n28|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n29|\n30|      - name: Set up Go\n31|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n32|        with:\n33|          go-version-file: go.mod\n34|\n35|      - name: Verify specification-to-code ownership\n36|        run: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n37|\n38|      # The diff proves the committed catalog matches generator output, but\n39|      # `go generate` runs nothing when its directive is disarmed: rewriting\n40|      # `//go:generate` as `// go:generate` preserves the token while turning\n41|      # the directive into a plain comment, so generation is skipped and the\n42|      # diff stays clean. The anchored check refuses that token-preserving\n43|      # rewrite; only the exact directive form counts. A new directive\n44|      # without a pin update reddens here (and in\n45|      # TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm) instead of going unchecked.\n46|      - name: Verify generated catalog is current\n47|        run: |\n48|          test \"$(grep -c '^//go:generate' internal/catalog/catalog.go)\" -eq 1\n49|          go generate ./internal/catalog\n50|          git diff --exit-code -- internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\n51|\n52|      # The release roots are derived from internal/specpin and\n53|      # internal/catalog inside the gate, never retyped here. Each -- PASS\n54|      # guard below must match: a selector that runs nothing fails here\n55|      # instead of passing silently.\n56|      - name: Run pinned contract-version gates\n57|        run: |\n58|          set +e\n59|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestVerifyContractPreservationLive|TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities|TestDerivedSetsAreComplete|TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets|TestCheckAgreementRefusals|TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift' -count=1 -v > cigate-contracts.log 2>&1\n60|          code=$?\n61|          set -e\n62|          cat cigate-contracts.log\n63|          test $code -eq 0\n64|          for gate in TestVerifyContractPreservationLive TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities TestDerivedSetsAreComplete TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets TestCheckAgreementRefusals TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift; do\n65|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-contracts.log\n66|          done\n67|\n68|  lint:\n69|    name: Linters (vet, Windows vet, gofmt)\n70|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n71|    timeout-minutes: 10\n72|    steps:\n73|      - name: Check out repository\n74|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n75|\n76|      - name: Set up Go\n77|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n78|        with:\n79|          go-version-file: go.mod\n80|\n81|      - name: Vet\n82|        run: go vet ./...\n83|\n84|      - name: Vet Windows build-tagged sources\n85|        run: GOOS=windows go vet ./...\n86|\n87|      # gofmt lists only offending files, so a clean tree prints nothing.\n88|      # The file count proves the scan was not empty; the log must then be.\n89|      - name: Check formatting\n90|        run: |\n91|          count=$(find internal -name '*.go' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\n92|          echo \"go files scanned: ${count}\"\n93|          test \"${count}\" -gt 0\n94|          set +e\n95|          gofmt -l internal > gofmt.log 2>&1\n96|          code=$?\n97|          set -e\n98|          cat gofmt.log\n99|          test $code -eq 0\n100|          test ! -s gofmt.log\n101|\n102|  test:\n103|    name: Build and test (no cache)\n104|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n105|    timeout-minutes: 15\n106|    steps:\n107|      - name: Check out repository\n108|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n109|\n110|      - name: Set up Go\n111|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n112|        with:\n113|          go-version-file: go.mod\n114|\n115|      - name: Build\n116|        run: go build ./...\n117|\n118|      # Verbose on purpose: the --- SKIP lines are the suite-wide skip\n119|      # datum. At least one package must report ok: a suite that matched\n120|      # nothing is a failure, not a pass.\n121|      - name: Test\n122|        run: |\n123|          set +e\n124|          go test ./... -v -count=1 > test.log 2>&1\n125|          code=$?\n126|          set -e\n127|          cat test.log\n128|          test $code -eq 0\n129|          test \"$(grep -c '^ok' test.log)\" -gt 0\n130|          test \"$(grep -c '^FAIL' test.log || true)\" -eq 0\n131|          {\n132|            echo \"## Suite skips\"\n133|            echo \"\"\n134|            echo \"Skipped: $(grep -c '^--- SKIP' test.log || true)\"\n135|            grep '^--- SKIP' test.log || echo \"none\"\n136|          } >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n137|\n138|  race:\n139|    name: Race detector\n140|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n141|    timeout-minutes: 15\n142|    steps:\n143|      - name: Check out repository\n144|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n145|\n146|      - name: Set up Go\n147|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n148|        with:\n149|          go-version-file: go.mod\n150|\n151|      - name: Test with race detector\n152|        run: |\n153|          set +e\n154|          go test -race ./... -count=1 > race.log 2>&1\n155|          code=$?\n156|          set -e\n157|          cat race.log\n158|          test $code -eq 0\n159|          test \"$(grep -c '^ok' race.log)\" -gt 0\n160|\n161|  coverage:\n162|    name: Coverage numbers (reported, no floor)\n163|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n164|    timeout-minutes: 15\n165|    steps:\n166|      - name: Check out repository\n167|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n168|\n169|      - name: Set up Go\n170|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n171|        with:\n172|          go-version-file: go.mod\n173|\n174|      # Coverage is a number, not a gate: this job reports per-package\n175|      # percentages and refuses only an unreadable or empty result.\n176|      - name: Test with coverage\n177|        run: |\n178|          set +e\n179|          go test ./... -cover -count=1 > cover.log 2>&1\n180|          code=$?\n181|          set -e\n182|          cat cover.log\n183|          test $code -eq 0\n184|          test \"$(grep -c 'coverage: ' cover.log)\" -gt 0\n185|          {\n186|            echo \"## Coverage\"\n187|            echo \"\"\n188|            echo \"| Package | Coverage |\"\n189|            echo \"| --- | --- |\"\n190|            grep 'coverage: ' cover.log | sed -E 's/^(ok|---)[[:space:]]+([^[:space:]]+).*coverage: ([0-9.]+% of statements)/| `\\2` | \\3 |/' || true\n191|            echo \"\"\n192|            echo \"Packages without test files (stated bounds, not failures):\"\n193|            echo \"\"\n194|            grep 'no test files' cover.log || echo \"none\"\n195|          } >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n196|\n197|  fixture-matrix:\n198|    name: Conformance fixtures (${{ matrix.os }}, ${{ matrix.package }})\n199|    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n200|    timeout-minutes: 15\n201|    strategy:\n202|      fail-fast: false\n203|      matrix:\n204|        os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest]\n205|        package: [internal/secprim, internal/secconftest]\n206|    steps:\n207|      - name: Check out repository\n208|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n209|\n210|      - name: Set up Go\n211|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n212|        with:\n213|          go-version-file: go.mod\n214|\n215|      # Verbose on purpose: the --- SKIP lines are the skip datum, and the\n216|      # secconftest capabilities line witnesses the probe counters after the\n217|      # whole suite. Skips are loud here by construction.\n218|      - name: Run fixture package\n219|        run: |\n220|          set +e\n221|          go test ./${{ matrix.package }} -count=1 -v > fixture.log 2>&1\n222|          code=$?\n223|          set -e\n224|          grep '^--- SKIP' fixture.log || echo \"no skipped tests\"\n225|          grep 'secconftest capabilities on' fixture.log || true\n226|          {\n227|            echo \"## Fixture run ${{ matrix.os }} ${{ matrix.package }}\"\n228|            echo \"\"\n229|            echo \"Skipped: $(grep -c '^--- SKIP' fixture.log || true)\"\n230|          } >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n231|          test $code -eq 0\n232|          test \"$(grep -c '^--- PASS' fixture.log)\" -gt 0\n233|\n234|  fuzz-smoke:\n235|    name: Fuzz smoke (derived targets)\n236|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n237|    timeout-minutes: 15\n238|    steps:\n239|      - name: Check out repository\n240|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n241|\n242|      - name: Set up Go\n243|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n244|        with:\n245|          go-version-file: go.mod\n246|\n247|      # Targets are derived per package from the compiled test binaries,\n248|      # never retyped: only names starting with Fuzz are fuzz targets. An\n249|      # empty leg fails the total-count pin below: the grep sits in a\n250|      # pipeline whose exit status the shell discards, so it refuses\n251|      # nothing, and the non-empty-file check refuses only the\n252|      # every-package-empty case — a single silently empty package dies\n253|      # only at the pinned total. A new fuzz target without a CI update\n254|      # reddens here instead of going unsmoked.\n255|      - name: Derive fuzz targets\n256|        run: |\n257|          rm -f fuzz-targets.clean\n258|          for pkg in internal/secconftest internal/canonicaljson internal/scalar; do\n259|            go test \"./${pkg}\" -list '^Fuzz' > \"fuzz-targets-$(basename \"${pkg}\").log\" 2>&1\n260|            grep '^Fuzz' \"fuzz-targets-$(basename \"${pkg}\").log\" | sed \"s|^|${pkg} |\" >> fuzz-targets.clean\n261|          done\n262|          test -s fuzz-targets.clean\n263|          test \"$(wc -l < fuzz-targets.clean | tr -d ' ')\" -eq 13\n264|          cat fuzz-targets.clean\n265|\n266|      # The secconftest leg of that list must equal the cigate.FuzzTargets\n267|      # derivation, which maps each target to the production entry it\n268|      # drives. Either side drifting — a target without an entry, or an\n269|      # entry without a target — fails the diff before any smoke runs.\n270|      - name: Check secconftest list matches the target derivation\n271|        run: |\n272|          set +e\n273|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation|TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted' -count=1 -v > cigate-targets.log 2>&1\n274|          code=$?\n275|          set -e\n276|          cat cigate-targets.log\n277|          test $code -eq 0\n278|          for gate in TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted; do\n279|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-targets.log\n280|          done\n281|\n282|      # A -fuzz selector that matches nothing exits 0 with \"no fuzz tests\n283|      # to fuzz\", so exit status alone cannot prove execution. The\n284|      # '^fuzz: elapsed' line proves the engine ran; its absence fails.\n285|      # It does not prove the mutation phase: at -fuzztime=100x the\n286|      # large-corpus targets (secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus, all four\n287|      # canonicaljson targets) spend the budget on baseline coverage and\n288|      # never print 'now fuzzing'. Lengthening the budget or shrinking a\n289|      # corpus changes that without reddening here.\n290|      - name: Smoke each target\n291|        run: |\n292|          while read -r pkg target; do\n293|            go test \"./${pkg}\" -run='^$' -fuzz=\"^${target}$\" -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1 -count=1 > \"fuzz-$(basename \"${pkg}\")-${target}.log\" 2>&1\n294|            grep -q '^fuzz: elapsed' \"fuzz-$(basename \"${pkg}\")-${target}.log\"\n295|          done < fuzz-targets.clean\n296|\n297|  capability-claims:\n298|    name: Unsupported-capability claim check\n299|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n300|    timeout-minutes: 10\n301|    steps:\n302|      - name: Check out repository\n303|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n304|\n305|      - name: Set up Go\n306|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n307|        with:\n308|          go-version-file: go.mod\n309|\n310|      # The vocabulary is secconftest's probe set; the gate scans the README\n311|      # with every probe forced unavailable — the strongest posture, and\n312|      # host-independent: a backticked capability mention that reads as a\n313|      # positive availability claim is refused no matter what this host's\n314|      # probes would report. CheckAdvertisements reads ProbeState.Available\n315|      # from the states it is given, and both postures are driven\n316|      # (TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim forces all unavailable,\n317|      # TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable forces all available). What\n318|      # reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome:\n319|      # ProbeStates feeds only CapabilityIDs, which keeps the IDs and\n320|      # drops availability. README prose is never capability evidence\n321|      # either way.\n322|      - name: Check README with all probes forced unavailable\n323|        run: |\n324|          set +e\n325|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim|TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable|TestCapabilityIDsAreDerivedSorted|TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused|TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted|TestUnclassifiedMentionIsRefused' -count=1 -v > cigate-claims.log 2>&1\n326|          code=$?\n327|          set -e\n328|          cat cigate-claims.log\n329|          test $code -eq 0\n330|          for gate in TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable TestCapabilityIDsAreDerivedSorted TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted TestUnclassifiedMentionIsRefused; do\n331|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-claims.log\n332|          done\n333|\n334|  windows-compile-only:\n335|    name: Windows compile-only (no execution implied)\n336|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n337|    timeout-minutes: 10\n338|    steps:\n339|      - name: Check out repository\n340|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n341|\n342|      - name: Set up Go\n343|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n344|        with:\n345|          go-version-file: go.mod\n346|\n347|      # Compile-and-vet only: go vet type-checks test files as well, and no\n348|      # step here executes a Windows binary. A green here must never be read\n349|      # as behaviour executed on Windows.\n350|      - name: Compile for Windows\n351|        run: GOOS=windows go build ./...\n352|\n353|      - name: Vet Windows build (includes test files)\n354|        run: GOOS=windows go vet ./...\n355|\n356|  gates-verdict:\n357|    name: All gates green, none skipped\n358|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n359|    timeout-minutes: 5\n360|    needs:\n361|      - contract-preservation\n362|      - lint\n363|      - test\n364|      - race\n365|      - coverage\n366|      - fixture-matrix\n367|      - fuzz-smoke\n368|      - capability-claims\n369|      - windows-compile-only\n370|    if: always()\n371|    steps:\n372|      - name: Refuse any non-success dependency\n373|        run: |\n374|          echo '${{ toJSON(needs) }}' > needs.json\n375|          jq . needs.json\n376|          jq -e 'to_entries | map(select(.value.result != \"success\")) | length == 0' needs.json","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":545,"recorded_at":1780531400001085,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae3b-e664-7a03-b8a7-130cfc4d923d"},"task_id":"01a0ae3b-e664-7a03-b8a7-130cfc4d923d","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae3b-e664-7a03-b8a7-130cfc4d923d"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":546,"recorded_at":1780531400001087,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae3be24a76678af7f197a230ab1b","text":"Read text file `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n1|name: CI\n2|\n3|on:\n4|  pull_request:\n5|  push:\n6|    branches:\n7|      - main\n8|\n9|permissions:\n10|  contents: read\n11|\n12|# What green means. Every job below proves its selection matched something:\n13|# a grep, glob, file scan, matrix expansion, or test selector that finds\n14|# nothing fails closed instead of passing on an empty result set. No job\n15|# declares an `if:` condition, so no job can skip quietly; gates-verdict\n16|# additionally refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\n17|#\n18|# GOOS=windows work is compile-and-vet only. A green windows-compile-only job\n19|# proves the tree type-checks for Windows; it never implies executed\n20|# behaviour. Coverage is reported as numbers, not enforced as a floor.\n21|jobs:\n22|  contract-preservation:\n23|    name: Contract preservation (v0.5.0 current, v0.4.3 historical)\n24|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n25|    timeout-minutes: 10\n26|    steps:\n27|      - name: Check out repository\n28|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n29|\n30|      - name: Set up Go\n31|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n32|        with:\n33|          go-version-file: go.mod\n34|\n35|      - name: Verify specification-to-code ownership\n36|        run: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n37|\n38|      # The diff proves the committed catalog matches generator output, but\n39|      # `go generate` runs nothing when its directive is disarmed: rewriting\n40|      # `//go:generate` as `// go:generate` preserves the token while turning\n41|      # the directive into a plain comment, so generation is skipped and the\n42|      # diff stays clean. The anchored check refuses that token-preserving\n43|      # rewrite; only the exact directive form counts. A new directive\n44|      # without a pin update reddens here (and in\n45|      # TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm) instead of going unchecked.\n46|      - name: Verify generated catalog is current\n47|        run: |\n48|          test \"$(grep -c '^//go:generate' internal/catalog/catalog.go)\" -eq 1\n49|          go generate ./internal/catalog\n50|          git diff --exit-code -- internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\n51|\n52|      # The release roots are derived from internal/specpin and\n53|      # internal/catalog inside the gate, never retyped here. Each -- PASS\n54|      # guard below must match: a selector that runs nothing fails here\n55|      # instead of passing silently.\n56|      - name: Run pinned contract-version gates\n57|        run: |\n58|          set +e\n59|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestVerifyContractPreservationLive|TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities|TestDerivedSetsAreComplete|TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets|TestCheckAgreementRefusals|TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift' -count=1 -v > cigate-contracts.log 2>&1\n60|          code=$?\n61|          set -e\n62|          cat cigate-contracts.log\n63|          test $code -eq 0\n64|          for gate in TestVerifyContractPreservationLive TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities TestDerivedSetsAreComplete TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets TestCheckAgreementRefusals TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift; do\n65|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-contracts.log\n66|          done\n67|\n68|  lint:\n69|    name: Linters (vet, Windows vet, gofmt)\n70|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n71|    timeout-minutes: 10\n72|    steps:\n73|      - name: Check out repository\n74|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n75|\n76|      - name: Set up Go\n77|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n78|        with:\n79|          go-version-file: go.mod\n80|\n81|      - name: Vet\n82|        run: go vet ./...\n83|\n84|      - name: Vet Windows build-tagged sources\n85|        run: GOOS=windows go vet ./...\n86|\n87|      # gofmt lists only offending files, so a clean tree prints nothing.\n88|      # The file count proves the scan was not empty; the log must then be.\n89|      - name: Check formatting\n90|        run: |\n91|          count=$(find internal -name '*.go' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\n92|          echo \"go files scanned: ${count}\"\n93|          test \"${count}\" -gt 0\n94|          set +e\n95|          gofmt -l internal > gofmt.log 2>&1\n96|          code=$?\n97|          set -e\n98|          cat gofmt.log\n99|          test $code -eq 0\n100|          test ! -s gofmt.log\n101|\n102|  test:\n103|    name: Build and test (no cache)\n104|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n105|    timeout-minutes: 15\n106|    steps:\n107|      - name: Check out repository\n108|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n109|\n110|      - name: Set up Go\n111|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n112|        with:\n113|          go-version-file: go.mod\n114|\n115|      - name: Build\n116|        run: go build ./...\n117|\n118|      # Verbose on purpose: the --- SKIP lines are the suite-wide skip\n119|      # datum. At least one package must report ok: a suite that matched\n120|      # nothing is a failure, not a pass.\n121|      - name: Test\n122|        run: |\n123|          set +e\n124|          go test ./... -v -count=1 > test.log 2>&1\n125|          code=$?\n126|          set -e\n127|          cat test.log\n128|          test $code -eq 0\n129|          test \"$(grep -c '^ok' test.log)\" -gt 0\n130|          test \"$(grep -c '^FAIL' test.log || true)\" -eq 0\n131|          {\n132|            echo \"## Suite skips\"\n133|            echo \"\"\n134|            echo \"Skipped: $(grep -c '^--- SKIP' test.log || true)\"\n135|            grep '^--- SKIP' test.log || echo \"none\"\n136|          } >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n137|\n138|  race:\n139|    name: Race detector\n140|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n141|    timeout-minutes: 15\n142|    steps:\n143|      - name: Check out repository\n144|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n145|\n146|      - name: Set up Go\n147|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n148|        with:\n149|          go-version-file: go.mod\n150|\n151|      - name: Test with race detector\n152|        run: |\n153|          set +e\n154|          go test -race ./... -count=1 > race.log 2>&1\n155|          code=$?\n156|          set -e\n157|          cat race.log\n158|          test $code -eq 0\n159|          test \"$(grep -c '^ok' race.log)\" -gt 0\n160|\n161|  coverage:\n162|    name: Coverage numbers (reported, no floor)\n163|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n164|    timeout-minutes: 15\n165|    steps:\n166|      - name: Check out repository\n167|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n168|\n169|      - name: Set up Go\n170|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n171|        with:\n172|          go-version-file: go.mod\n173|\n174|      # Coverage is a number, not a gate: this job reports per-package\n175|      # percentages and refuses only an unreadable or empty result.\n176|      - name: Test with coverage\n177|        run: |\n178|          set +e\n179|          go test ./... -cover -count=1 > cover.log 2>&1\n180|          code=$?\n181|          set -e\n182|          cat cover.log\n183|          test $code -eq 0\n184|          test \"$(grep -c 'coverage: ' cover.log)\" -gt 0\n185|          {\n186|            echo \"## Coverage\"\n187|            echo \"\"\n188|            echo \"| Package | Coverage |\"\n189|            echo \"| --- | --- |\"\n190|            grep 'coverage: ' cover.log | sed -E 's/^(ok|---)[[:space:]]+([^[:space:]]+).*coverage: ([0-9.]+% of statements)/| `\\2` | \\3 |/' || true\n191|            echo \"\"\n192|            echo \"Packages without test files (stated bounds, not failures):\"\n193|            echo \"\"\n194|            grep 'no test files' cover.log || echo \"none\"\n195|          } >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n196|\n197|  fixture-matrix:\n198|    name: Conformance fixtures (${{ matrix.os }}, ${{ matrix.package }})\n199|    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n200|    timeout-minutes: 15\n201|    strategy:\n202|      fail-fast: false\n203|      matrix:\n204|        os: [ubuntu-latest, macos-latest]\n205|        package: [internal/secprim, internal/secconftest]\n206|    steps:\n207|      - name: Check out repository\n208|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n209|\n210|      - name: Set up Go\n211|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n212|        with:\n213|          go-version-file: go.mod\n214|\n215|      # Verbose on purpose: the --- SKIP lines are the skip datum, and the\n216|      # secconftest capabilities line witnesses the probe counters after the\n217|      # whole suite. Skips are loud here by construction.\n218|      - name: Run fixture package\n219|        run: |\n220|          set +e\n221|          go test ./${{ matrix.package }} -count=1 -v > fixture.log 2>&1\n222|          code=$?\n223|          set -e\n224|          grep '^--- SKIP' fixture.log || echo \"no skipped tests\"\n225|          grep 'secconftest capabilities on' fixture.log || true\n226|          {\n227|            echo \"## Fixture run ${{ matrix.os }} ${{ matrix.package }}\"\n228|            echo \"\"\n229|            echo \"Skipped: $(grep -c '^--- SKIP' fixture.log || true)\"\n230|          } >> \"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY\"\n231|          test $code -eq 0\n232|          test \"$(grep -c '^--- PASS' fixture.log)\" -gt 0\n233|\n234|  fuzz-smoke:\n235|    name: Fuzz smoke (derived targets)\n236|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n237|    timeout-minutes: 15\n238|    steps:\n239|      - name: Check out repository\n240|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n241|\n242|      - name: Set up Go\n243|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n244|        with:\n245|          go-version-file: go.mod\n246|\n247|      # Targets are derived per package from the compiled test binaries,\n248|      # never retyped: only names starting with Fuzz are fuzz targets. An\n249|      # empty leg fails the total-count pin below: the grep sits in a\n250|      # pipeline whose exit status the shell discards, so it refuses\n251|      # nothing, and the non-empty-file check refuses only the\n252|      # every-package-empty case — a single silently empty package dies\n253|      # only at the pinned total. A new fuzz target without a CI update\n254|      # reddens here instead of going unsmoked.\n255|      - name: Derive fuzz targets\n256|        run: |\n257|          rm -f fuzz-targets.clean\n258|          for pkg in internal/secconftest internal/canonicaljson internal/scalar; do\n259|            go test \"./${pkg}\" -list '^Fuzz' > \"fuzz-targets-$(basename \"${pkg}\").log\" 2>&1\n260|            grep '^Fuzz' \"fuzz-targets-$(basename \"${pkg}\").log\" | sed \"s|^|${pkg} |\" >> fuzz-targets.clean\n261|          done\n262|          test -s fuzz-targets.clean\n263|          test \"$(wc -l < fuzz-targets.clean | tr -d ' ')\" -eq 13\n264|          cat fuzz-targets.clean\n265|\n266|      # The secconftest leg of that list must equal the cigate.FuzzTargets\n267|      # derivation, which maps each target to the production entry it\n268|      # drives. Either side drifting — a target without an entry, or an\n269|      # entry without a target — fails the diff before any smoke runs.\n270|      - name: Check secconftest list matches the target derivation\n271|        run: |\n272|          set +e\n273|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation|TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted' -count=1 -v > cigate-targets.log 2>&1\n274|          code=$?\n275|          set -e\n276|          cat cigate-targets.log\n277|          test $code -eq 0\n278|          for gate in TestListedTargetsMatchDerivation TestFuzzTargetsAreDerivedSorted; do\n279|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-targets.log\n280|          done\n281|\n282|      # A -fuzz selector that matches nothing exits 0 with \"no fuzz tests\n283|      # to fuzz\", so exit status alone cannot prove execution. The\n284|      # '^fuzz: elapsed' line proves the engine ran; its absence fails.\n285|      # It does not prove the mutation phase: at -fuzztime=100x the\n286|      # large-corpus targets (secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus, all four\n287|      # canonicaljson targets) spend the budget on baseline coverage and\n288|      # never print 'now fuzzing'. Lengthening the budget or shrinking a\n289|      # corpus changes that without reddening here.\n290|      - name: Smoke each target\n291|        run: |\n292|          while read -r pkg target; do\n293|            go test \"./${pkg}\" -run='^$' -fuzz=\"^${target}$\" -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1 -count=1 > \"fuzz-$(basename \"${pkg}\")-${target}.log\" 2>&1\n294|            grep -q '^fuzz: elapsed' \"fuzz-$(basename \"${pkg}\")-${target}.log\"\n295|          done < fuzz-targets.clean\n296|\n297|  capability-claims:\n298|    name: Unsupported-capability claim check\n299|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n300|    timeout-minutes: 10\n301|    steps:\n302|      - name: Check out repository\n303|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n304|\n305|      - name: Set up Go\n306|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n307|        with:\n308|          go-version-file: go.mod\n309|\n310|      # The vocabulary is secconftest's probe set; the gate scans the README\n311|      # with every probe forced unavailable — the strongest posture, and\n312|      # host-independent: a backticked capability mention that reads as a\n313|      # positive availability claim is refused no matter what this host's\n314|      # probes would report. CheckAdvertisements reads ProbeState.Available\n315|      # from the states it is given, and both postures are driven\n316|      # (TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim forces all unavailable,\n317|      # TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable forces all available). What\n318|      # reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome:\n319|      # ProbeStates feeds only CapabilityIDs, which keeps the IDs and\n320|      # drops availability. README prose is never capability evidence\n321|      # either way.\n322|      - name: Check README with all probes forced unavailable\n323|        run: |\n324|          set +e\n325|          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim|TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable|TestCapabilityIDsAreDerivedSorted|TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused|TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted|TestUnclassifiedMentionIsRefused' -count=1 -v > cigate-claims.log 2>&1\n326|          code=$?\n327|          set -e\n328|          cat cigate-claims.log\n329|          test $code -eq 0\n330|          for gate in TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim TestRealREADMEAdmitsWhenAllAvailable TestCapabilityIDsAreDerivedSorted TestPositiveClaimsAreRefused TestNegatedClaimsAreAdmitted TestUnclassifiedMentionIsRefused; do\n331|            grep -q \"^--- PASS: ${gate}\" cigate-claims.log\n332|          done\n333|\n334|  windows-compile-only:\n335|    name: Windows compile-only (no execution implied)\n336|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n337|    timeout-minutes: 10\n338|    steps:\n339|      - name: Check out repository\n340|        uses: actions/checkout@v7\n341|\n342|      - name: Set up Go\n343|        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\n344|        with:\n345|          go-version-file: go.mod\n346|\n347|      # Compile-and-vet only: go vet type-checks test files as well, and no\n348|      # step here executes a Windows binary. A green here must never be read\n349|      # as behaviour executed on Windows.\n350|      - name: Compile for Windows\n351|        run: GOOS=windows go build ./...\n352|\n353|      - name: Vet Windows build (includes test files)\n354|        run: GOOS=windows go vet ./...\n355|\n356|  gates-verdict:\n357|    name: All gates green, none skipped\n358|    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n359|    timeout-minutes: 5\n360|    needs:\n361|      - contract-preservation\n362|      - lint\n363|      - test\n364|      - race\n365|      - coverage\n366|      - fixture-matrix\n367|      - fuzz-smoke\n368|      - capability-claims\n369|      - windows-compile-only\n370|    if: always()\n371|    steps:\n372|      - name: Refuse any non-success dependency\n373|        run: |\n374|          echo '${{ toJSON(needs) }}' > needs.json\n375|          jq . needs.json\n376|          jq -e 'to_entries | map(select(.value.result != \"success\")) | length == 0' needs.json","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
