{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c899","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":679,"recorded_at":1780531400001353,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae3c-4c17-76d2-b80f-2091d6ac3278"},"task_id":"01a0ae3c-4c17-76d2-b80f-2091d6ac3278","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae3c-4c17-76d2-b80f-2091d6ac3278","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2674 line(s) above)\n2675|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n2676|go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n2677|```\n2678|\n2679|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n2680|\n2681|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n2682|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n2683|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n2684|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n2685|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 110\n2686|executable acceptance cases, 57 exact section bindings with their declared\n2687|coverage, 11 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n2688|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n2689|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n2690|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n2691|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n2692|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n2693|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n2694|\n2695|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n2696|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n2697|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n2698|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n2699|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n2700|build:\n2701|\n2702|```bash\n2703|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n2704|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
