{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c89d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":681,"recorded_at":1780531400001357,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae3c44157196a0aa844dbe27c051","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-21-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"gap\\\" internal/traceability/traceability.go | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate gap validation rules\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"97:// assigned-scope admission refuses an unowned section and prints its gap.\\n100:\\tGap      string `json:\\\"gap\\\"`\\n124:\\tGap             string             `json:\\\"gap,omitempty\\\"`\\n160:\\t// carries the same mandatory gap as every other level below full and is\\n990:// minimumGapLength is the shortest gap sentence the gate accepts. A gap has to\\n994:// verifyGapDiscloses checks that a gap sentence is a disclosure rather than\\n996:// not fully covered here yet.\\\" satisfied both while saying nothing. A real gap\\n1000:// gap about 6.55 cannot pass for a gap about 6.5.\\n1005:func verifyGapDiscloses(gap, display, declaration string) error {\\n1006:\\tif len(gap) < minimumGapLength {\\n1007:\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"gap %q is shorter than the %d characters a disclosure needs\\\", gap, minimumGapLength)\\n1009:\\tif !mentionsSection(gap, display) {\\n1010:\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"gap does not name section %s as a whole identifier\\\", display)\\n1012:\\tif declaration != \\\"\\\" && !strings.Contains(gap, declaration) {\\n1013:\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"gap does not name the production declaration %q the binding is registered to\\\", declaration)\\n1020:// \\\"6.5\\\" and \\\"13.15\\\" as a mention of \\\"13.1\\\", which would let a gap about one\\n1047:// sectionDisplayName is how a gap sentence has to name the section it is about.\\n1223:\\t// Every level below full owes a gap, coverageUnmeasured included. Before\\n1224:\\t// this the gate refused a gap on the unmeasured bucket, so the bindings with\\n1230:\\t\\t\\treturn sectionCoverage{}, fail(\\\"section binding %q claims %s coverage and still names a gap\\\", key, measured)\\n1262:// the generated catalog requires an owner for, and must state a gap and the\\n1293:\\t\\t// the gap is checked for length and a whole-identifier section mention\\n1299:\\t\\t\\treturn nil, fail(\\\"unowned section %q states no evidence for its gap\\\", entry.Key)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1794,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 449,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
