{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d2f5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":2005,"recorded_at":1780531400004005,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae49-583f-7a61-ab9f-d5a98f24a352"},"task_id":"01a0ae49-583f-7a61-ab9f-d5a98f24a352","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae49-583f-7a61-ab9f-d5a98f24a352","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1854 line(s) above)\n1855|go test ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -run '^TestCensusLiveEventOwnershipPlants$' -v\n1856|```\n1857|\n1858|The live test uses a temporary package copy and read-only dependency symlinks;\n1859|it restores its copied sources and never mutates the managed worktree. It runs\n1860|on the normal package suite and adds compiler/subprocess time. Task validation\n1861|logs and mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-1r9wrr`; scratch\n1862|outputs live under `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/`.\n1863|\n1864|## Provider and pane fencing gates\n1865|\n1866|[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing) gates every activation-class action on\n1867|the winning lease and the exact fencing epoch (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2,\n1868|5.3, and 13.6-13.10, the Section 4 terminal wrapper rule, and the Section 7.5\n1869|`LeaseToken`). `Observe` loads the winning lease through the `sessrepo` owner\n1870|and combines it with the caller's sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts;\n1871|`AuthorizeActivation`, `AuthorizeInput`, `AuthorizeMutation`,\n1872|`AuthorizeCheckpoint`, and `AuthorizeRestore` decide over that observation\n1873|through one core, and `AuthorizeTerminateStale` gates stale-process\n1874|termination. A passed gate mints a sealed `LeaseToken` that binds the exact\n1875|`{session_id, lease_epoch, lease_id}` triple to the `quiesce`, `capture`, and\n1876|`materialize` provider operations; a failed gate refuses with a Section 15\n1877|registered code and nothing else (`lease_conflict`, `not_owner`, `stale_owner`\n1878|at exit 10, `invalid_arguments` at exit 2, `local_precondition_failed` at\n1879|exit 3, proven by constructing each through `internal/axerror`). Launch-class\n1880|entries park instead of refusing when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1881|unverified, or absent, carrying the Section 5.2 `session.parked` vocabulary\n1882|(`remote_owner`, `stale_owner`, `restore_policy`, `failed_handoff`) with the\n1883|winning lease ID; every other entry refuses outright. Takeover, fork, stop,\n1884|and resume transactions are modeled as callers, not members: the gates own\n1885|their entry points only, and terminal backends and provider plugin processes\n1886|stay outside the package.\n1887|\n1888|The gates are pure over durable inputs: they perform no writes, hold no\n1889|cache, and read no clock except the caller-supplied reading, so there is no\n1890|crash seam and repeated evaluation decides identically. The sealed token has\n1891|no exported field or constructor — only the gate mints it — and an AST census\n1892|pins that boundary with comment/string controls plus an alias-backdoor plant\n1893|that preserves the searched-for token while changing the construction path.\n1894|\n1895|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n1896|\n1897|```bash\n1898|go test ./internal/fencing -count=1\n1899|go test ./internal/fencing -cover -count=1\n1900|```\n1901|\n1902|Run the narrowing battery (30 narrowing mutants plus one token-preserving\n1903|census mutant and three controls) with:\n1904|\n1905|```bash\n1906|python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\n1907|```\n1908|\n1909|The harness copies the tree, applies each plant, runs the named behavioral\n1910|tests (the full suite for the census mutant), and writes per-mutant logs with\n1911|real exits to `mutants.json`; it restores its copied sources and never\n1912|mutates the managed worktree. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n1913|attached to `TASK-260830-3g12yp`; scratch outputs live under\n1914|`.temp/TASK-260830-3g12yp/`. The package adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\n1915|result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its\n1916|stated bounds lives in\n1917|[the task evidence map](internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md).\n1918|\n1919|## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\n1920|\n1921|`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted\n1922|session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the\n1923|v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared\n1924|SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):\n1925|\n1926|- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare\n1927|  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the\n1928|  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,\n1929|  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
