{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d477","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":2198,"recorded_at":1780531400004391,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae4a0fec72edbf22928b2ac5dcce","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-60-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"^## \\\" LOGBOOK.md | tail -n 5; echo ===; sed -n \\\"$(grep -n '^## ' LOGBOOK.md | tail -n 1 | cut -d: -f1),+12p\\\" LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"See last LOGBOOK heading style\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"835:## 2026-09-04\\n895:## 2026-09-03\\n1188:## 2026-09-02\\n1430:## 2026-09-02 — BUG-260902-2faftr: a name blacklist is not secret detection\\n1497:## 2026-09-01\\n===\\n## 2026-09-01\\n\\n### 2340 — A self-consistent value is not a pinned value\\n\\n- ROOT CAUSE: `ProjectionMetadata.SourceFingerprint` was asserted only against itself across three opens of the same source. A constant is maximally self-consistent, so replacing `projectionSourceFingerprint` with `\\\"sha256:\\\" + hex(make([]byte, 32))` satisfied every existing assertion. The whole fingerprint chain — and the scan ordering feeding it — was reachable, exercised, and unfalsifiable.\\n- FINDING: The determinism test read digest order back through `Objects()`, which carries its own `ORDER BY storage_class, representation, digest`. The loop that looked like it pinned the production `sort.Slice` was decided by the read query in a different function. This is the round-6/7 sibling-decider shape again, one step further out: the decider is not a preceding line or a sibling term but a re-sort on the read path.\\n- DECISION: Derive the expected fingerprint *outside the module*. `.temp/TASK-260830-3amrl9/fingerprint-derivation.py` re-implements it in Python and executes no Go production code, so the golden cannot be a copy of what the implementation emits today. It independently reproduced the reviewer's probe value exactly.\\n- FINDING: The self-checking fixture earned its keep immediately. The table re-hashes each pinned content, and the first draft paired the contents with the wrong digests — caught on the first run, not by inspection.\\n- ANOMALY: `_defensive=1` in the DSN is honoured by modernc.org/sqlite (`SQLITE_DBCONFIG_DEFENSIVE`) and is the only thing stopping the live connection from rewriting `sqlite_master` — precisely the mutation the drift fixtures perform on raw connections. The word appeared exactly once in the whole change, on that DSN line. Two lines above, `_synchronous` carried a full subsumption note; the parameter that *was* individually observable had none.\\n- DECISION: A refusal test needs a forward control when the refusal could plausibly be the dependency's default. `TestOpenProjectionConnectionRefusesSchemaRewrites` asserts the same two statements *succeed* on a connection opened without `_defensive`, so the refusal is attributed to this projection's configuration rather than to SQLite baseline behaviour.\\n- DECISION: Extract the inline `sort.Slice` closure to `sortIndexedObjects` so the comparator can be driven directly with a same-digest pair. The scan can never produce that input — one digest owns one path under `digest_path_v1` — so the `RelativePath` tie-break was untestable while the comparator stayed inline.\\n- ANOMALY: Deleting the ordering *call* from `scanAuthoritativeBlobs` stays green and legitimately so: `os.ReadDir` returns filename-sorted entries and the shard split makes that traversal already ascending by digest. Genuine subsumption by a dependency's contract rather than by another check in the suite — documented at the call site, with the order itself pinned in both directions on the extracted comparator.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/localstore/projection_test.go` (3 new cases, self-checking fixture, independent fingerprint derivation), `internal/localstore/projection.go` (`sortIndexedObjects` extraction plus two call-site comments), `README.md`.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3378,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 845,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
