{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e1a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae38-1954-7242-9b52-ff7ca6c9b52f"},"sequence":3887,"recorded_at":1780531400007769,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"815552bd-492d-441d-89cf-fcae5a028cc4"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260830-2atgj4 is `to-review` with 14/14 checklist items and three outcome resources attached (`..._results.md`, `..._conformance-matrix.md`, `..._producer-evidence.tar.gz`, a real gzip with 49 members). The candidate is left uncommitted in the Story worktree (13 paths, verified).\n\nWhat was delivered:\n\n- **11 property tests** proving the four invariants over the landed reducers with hand-written closed-alphabet generators (no new dependency): union-order independence (2,907 exhaustive pairs + 2,000 seeded-random multisets, 63,050 `Reduce` calls) and partition stability (21,315 concatenations) in [ownership_properties_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree/internal/sessstate/ownership_properties_test.go); loser preservation; winner-is-maximum over 289 pairs / 4,913 triples; store clock non-authority (4 shifts + mixed chain) and single-authority-per-epoch (21 exhaustive + 200 seeded sequences) in [lease_properties_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree/internal/sessrepo/lease_properties_test.go); gate clock translation-invariance (80 authorizations) and exactly-one-owner with pairwise exclusion (150 authorizations) in [ownership_properties_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree/internal/fencing/ownership_properties_test.go). AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven, each with its production call site.\n- **One genuine defect found RED-first and fixed minimally**: `resolveWinner` reported losing leases against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's evidence could vanish depending on union order. The fix selects the greatest tuple first, then reports every entry below it in ascending order naming the final winner. RED log (4 of 5 fail) and GREEN log are in the tarball; all landed union assertions were order-free, so only census line pins moved.\n- **Falsification battery** [mutate_properties.py](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree/internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py): 8 narrowing plants, each KILLED by its named property (the expiry plant is invisible to the landed suite — only the translation property kills it); harmless control SURVIVED; harness exit 0.\n- **Story-close**: 3 traceability acceptance cases bound to `Reduce`/`WinningLease`/`Authorize` with unchanged coverage ratios, section:17.2 gap reworded to the reader-enum meaning, digest re-pinned (`63c8379…`), 110→113 pins updated, the 3g12yp P3 vector added, README property section + harness row, LOGBOOK entry.\n- **Full validation green**: vet/Windows-vet/gofmt/build/Windows-build, tracecheck (113 cases), cataloggen, cigate contracts + claims, all 27 test packages, race with no data races, coverage (sessstate 92.4%, sessrepo 86.6%, fencing 97.5%), fixture matrix, 13/13 fuzz smoke.\n\nTwo notes for the reviewer/integrator, both documented in the results: trunk moved during the run (STORY-260917-158jyi cataloggen change; `refresh-candidate` stops at a mechanical LOGBOOK conflict in the 2f5393 replay whose resolution-file schema isn't documented on any available surface — the candidate is intact and the merge notes are in the results), and row 10 of the DoD holds vacuously (no source-text gate shipped; the in-scope census keeps its landed token-preserving mutant).","reason":null}}
